                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Congrats to Oddgames on getting a title published! I personally know what it means to get something completed and on the market! As a single person developer it is an enormous accomplishment and something to be very very proud of!\n\nNow for the review!\nPros:\n- I love the scenary, the detail and the effects. The bookshelves, the furniture, the tiles and objects are very good.\n- Overall the graphics are good and satisfying for me. The cutscenes are great and the detailed portraits are fantastic\n- Personally I like the simplistic click actions\n- I am intrigued in the story. I loved the cutscenes and felt they did a decent job of pulling you in.\n- The fact that loot is the number one goal in order to get stronger is a good feature.\n- The UI Windows and the action bar look great. A bit on the simplistic side, but thats a good thing!\n\nCons:\n- Lack of a skill system\n- Lack of a crafting sytem\n\nOverall I give the game a very enthusiastic thumbs up! Yes, a skill system would ensure the games position as an RPG, but in reality a Role Playing Game means you assume the role of the character in the game and lead the character through the story, making decisions for him, that is all a RPG is in a nutshell. A skill system in my opinion is a definite feature we all love and a crafting system would definitely put things over the top!\n\nIn conclusion, be proud of what you have accomplished, listen to the critiques but don't take any immature remarks or comments to heart. After doing this for 15 years, you will see the trolls crawl out from under their bridges with no good criticisms and downright bullying attitudes along with a pack attack mentality. Don't get discouraged and be proud because you have made a major accomplishment here!",
